 # Calendar workflow implementation
 
-Status: ordinary event editor and approved UI refinement on the local `codex/calendar-workflows` branch, based on main `8539fe8`. Updated 31 October 2026.
+Status: active private implementation in `/Users/ali/Developer/warpdrive-calendar`, detached at `2803183` plus preserved local edits. Settings owns integration and required main checks. The full roadmap remains open; private qualification is not main delivery, installed-upgrade proof or real-provider acceptance. Updated 2 November 2026.
+
+## Current evidence, 2 November 2026
+
+The main-relative C-shortcut increment is Delivered as `a29c08c356af8a308056086ecbac98f2d70683e4`. Exact hosted CI `41365229340` passed all required jobs at 00:25:39 UTC on 2 November: 8,670 unit cases (3 skipped), 3,066 integration cases, full types/lint, application, all five worker bundles and sites. All thirteen shortcut component cases passed. This is source delivery; browser, installed-upgrade and provider acceptance remain open.
+
+The page visitor and collector share cumulative storage limits, validate whole pages before a sequential sink and preserve the captured readable role, error identity and abort reason. Actual private source passed 64 cases across ten files, configured type generation/typecheck and scoped checks on the full 24-file closure. Its add-only handoff is awaiting main integration. This supersedes the older unrun page-visitor preparation below; durable staging/cursor publication, Activity import, watch/sync workers and Meet provisioning remain open.
+
+The separate notification-INSERT failure/retry native case passed1/1 in3.23seconds, with a sequence witness, full rollback and same-UUID retry yielding one owner-visible receipt. This remains Date-only direct-handler proof. A later C-shortcut fix prevents a second editor when keyboard events bubble from a week/day portal:22component cases completed passing across the new, week-grid and isolated FA/DE/EN navigation files. The combined-run timeout is retained. The current UI then passed configured Next type generation/full TypeScript and typed lint with zero errors or warnings; actual browser qualification remains open. The product layout and CRM actions are unchanged.
+
+Completion input preserves canonical `E_ACTIVITY_008`, distinct conflict `E_ACTIVITY_009`, strict validation and optional positive revision. Contract tests passed 52/52 and affected UI tests passed 26/26, including removal of the editor's guessed next version. The initial PostgreSQL selection produced four passes and three intended completion replay failures. After the minimum authorization-preserving no-op fix and configured types/scoped lint, the separately allocated native GREEN passed all seven cases in4.29seconds: witnessed stale-reminder rollback, matching successful edit, Date-only direct reminder delivery/feed/unread, permission-before-no-op, zero-write same-state replay, concurrent canonical return and stale-token reminder-safe replay. Exact owned cleanup retained the three fresh baseline containers. This remains private-lineage logical SQL/direct-handler proof; no main, live worker, canonical upgrade or provider acceptance is implied.
+
+Canonical migrations 0000–0097 remain unchanged; 0098 is reserved and its native persistence/transition boundaries are accepted, but no SQL is authored. The accepted design requires a separate legacy/intent ownership field, persisted suppression, shared Activity locking for takeover/legacy delivery, separate intent queue and incompatible-consumer fencing, authentic historical receipt visibility, and current durable email admission. The three-case engine diagnostic reached three intended assertion failures with no setup failures: legacy rebuild created native work, and both new native create paths persisted the wrong legacy marker after their other controls passed. After the minimal persistence/reconciliation fix, configured application types and scoped fixture/lint closure, eleven selected native cases passed, including the original three and affected delivery/rebuild/concurrency/batching controls. The initial fixture-configuration type failure is retained. The local live-acceptance adapters are type/lint-qualified and remain runtime-unrun. Exact migration/legacy/installed acceptance remains open. The private native test lineage does not qualify that upgrade. The user has no Google OAuth/test-account setup yet and chose continued local implementation; actual Google Calendar/Meet acceptance remains separate.
+
+The historical reminder visibility correction is now privately qualified. After the authentic producer/feed/unread assertion first failed, all 22 selected cases across four files passed, with 30 deliberately unselected and zero setup failures. Configured Next route generation/full application TypeScript, scoped fixture types and typed lint for one production plus three fixture/config paths passed with no errors or warnings. The same receipt remains visible when automation is disabled, while actual email admission remains suppressed; current CRM/calendar, malformed-reference/backlink and modern suppression controls passed. Exact cleanup retained all three fresh foreign containers and all 21 source pins. Total allocation including observed cleanup was 101.25 seconds. This does not establish canonical upgrade, native engine admission, queue separation, owner adoption, compatible takeover/receipt transfer, live workers, browser or provider acceptance.
+
+The populated upgrade diagnostic has now reached its intended failure after successful migration and all preservation controls. Exact canonical 0000–0097 and its 98-entry ledger were followed by the historical private native test input. The resulting 99-entry ledger, old Activity/notification/CRM snapshots, legacy ownership, version and authorship controls passed. The copied Calendar backfills then left one unadmitted pending dual-channel intent and one dirty marker for an old event. No delivery or provider effect occurred. Runner time was 4.02 seconds; exact container/process/temp-root cleanup retained all three foreign baselines and all 29 source pins. The later native-create control was not reached.
+
+The corrected new private test migration omits only those two blanket INSERTs, retains the original historical fragments/manifest and unchanged case, and leaves all 98 canonical migrations byte-identical. Public canonical 0085/0087 are unrelated Privacy/Integration migrations; the Calendar names are old private fragments, not admitted canonical history. Current 32 hashes and commands are in `Calendar_Canonical_Upgrade_No_Activation_Preparation_2026-11-02/prepared.json`. Source review, formatting and actual SQL-folder assembly passed. Fresh scoped fixture types/helper lint then passed, and the same populated-upgrade case passed in 3.77 seconds, including the previously unreached actual native calendar/event create and one pending in-app-only intent. Old migration data and all source pins were preserved; exact cleanup retained the three fresh foreign baselines and removed the owned process/container/temp roots. Overall allocation was 65.33 seconds, with independent post-native verification in 33.14 seconds. `Calendar_Canonical_Upgrade_GREEN1_2026-11-02/result.json` records this qualified private cut. This does not admit canonical SQL or qualify installed data, queue ownership, legacy takeover, final MAIL admission, live workers, browser or providers.
+
+### Earlier checkpoint and historical receipts
+
+The current [continuation checkpoint, 1 November 2026](calendar-progress-2026-11-01.md) records local implementation, verification and remaining gates; the earlier [31 October handoff](calendar-handoff-2026-10-31.md) retains foundation/restart details. Transactional reminder intent fixes the missing-queue partial-save blocker, and reminder cutoff integrity passed its 152-case native selection and populated-fixture migration 0090. Earlier 28-case account/UI and unconfigured Farsi/German browser proof retain their scope, alongside 69 native OAuth/cookie/admission and 17 pure collector milestones. Current durable catalog/selection, clock and source-guard evidence is 152 affected native cases across 25 files in 25.31 seconds. The account/UI return passed 53 cases across seven files in 2.21 seconds, including 25 panel/query cases and the disconnect-cache correction. Fresh full types and scoped checks on 50 TypeScript plus three locale JSON files passed. Opening the catalog performs no provider discovery; saved selection does not import events or enable synchronization/Meet. Synthetic Farsi/German desktop/mobile browser/server/database acceptance now covers stable Add/Remove/re-Add, availability-only Add denial and disconnect hiding metadata, with exact fixture cleanup, restored preferences/viewport and unchanged environment/source. The app stopped; its shutdown wrapper's post-stop EPERM probe is a separate harness limitation, with the process group and port independently confirmed empty. Disconnected-account binding-management UI remains future work. The preserved-fixture 0092 upgrade retained every original event/calendar field/version. Candidate numbering remains unreserved; real app/test-user setup, configured provider acceptance, an accepted combined cut and installed-upgrade qualification remain open. The raw-event bounds package is promoted after an initial nine-policy-failure/three-control RED, four later cursor failures with twelve controls, and ignored 16/16 candidate GREEN in 384 ms. An unchanged-body test split leaves six source files. Current pure-transport qualification passed 53/53 affected units across seven files in 715 ms (sixteen new cases across three files plus 37 controls), scoped Biome/typed ESLint for all six TypeScript files and full types in a 3.04-second owned wrapper, with all 64 inputs conserved and owned groups empty. This package did not repeat native, build or browser acceptance. Its Warpdrive policies cap 1,000 pages, 50,000 events, 1 MiB per raw event, 32 MiB aggregate event JSON, depth 32, 64 KiB per returned cursor and 1 MiB retained page tokens, rejecting unsafe Unicode and exact duplicate IDs. Only complete successful collection returns a final cursor; no durable mirror, import, background sync, real-provider or streaming HTTP/peak-memory qualification follows. The next ignored nine-case/two-file retention preparation and eleven-case page-visitor preparation remain unrun. The full roadmap remains active, with Google Calendar and Google Meet the first provider integration/acceptance target.
 
 The product target is the Google Calendar desktop workflow described in [the reference inventory](google-calendar-event-workflow.md). Preserve Warpdrive's current shell, CRM relationships, permission checks, Farsi and German support, independent calendar preferences and Iranian date pickers. This document records implementation progress; it does not claim full Google Calendar parity.
 
@@ -27,7 +49,7 @@ The user approved the design direction after a logged-in Mobbin review. The stro
 Implemented using Warpdrive's existing components, fonts and tokens:
 
 - A prominent event title and grouped start/end controls lead the form. Location and description can be revealed when needed in compact mode.
-- Expanding the same draft adds a separate CRM details column containing the real activity type, priority, accessible linked records and preserved participant counts. On narrow screens this column follows event details in the scrollable body; the save/cancel footer remains available.
+- The latest user refinement keeps one compact primary column. Calendar settings, authored time-zone selection and CRM details reveal inline, with selected-calendar and non-default summaries visible while collapsed. The permanent sidebar and wide expansion have been removed; the save/cancel footer remains available.
 - Meeting links appear as a provider/hostname summary with join, copy, edit and remove controls. The inline editor validates HTTPS links, rejects URL credentials and applies changes to the draft without saving the event. Escape cancels only the link edit. Query strings and fragments are omitted from the summary.
 - Description styling is neutral, with formatting controls revealed on focus or through an explicit toggle. Completion/reopening and deletion live in the event actions menu.
 - Ctrl/Command+Enter saves the event after committing a visible time draft. Invalid clock input blocks submission. Farsi retains RTL layout, Iranian dates and Persian digits; German receives the same workflow with contextual terminology.
