 ## 3. Validation and limitations
 
+The following paragraphs retain the earlier UI checkpoint. Later signed-in local delivery, personal reminder defaults/overrides and dedicated Google OAuth work are recorded in [1 November continuation evidence](calendar-progress-2026-11-01.md). The full roadmap remains active; local OAuth and reminder tests do not establish real provider acceptance or completion of the other workflows.
+
 The first slice has unit coverage for Farsi/German/English draft continuity, Persian digits, dates, DST and untouched timestamp preservation; calendar entry points and record links; stale-cache/read-failure behavior; existing completion/follow-up handling; and save-failure draft retention.
 
 Real PostgreSQL 16 tests exercise Farsi/German create, reopen and edit round trips for timed and all-day events, canonical civil dates across display-zone changes, and unrelated-user read/edit denial. The local check uses a disposable, separately initialized PostgreSQL instance because Docker is unavailable, with the repository's real migrations and test database helper. CI retains the normal Docker integration lane.
diff --git a/docs/deploy.md b/docs/deploy.md
index 71c0102..28949d7 100644
--- a/docs/deploy.md
+++ b/docs/deploy.md
@@ -94,8 +94,12 @@ Before upgrading an existing installation, follow the
 
 ## Operating the box
 
-- **Update to a new version:** `git pull && docker compose up -d --build`. Migrations run
-  automatically via the one-shot `migrate` service before the app restarts.
+- **Update to a new version:** build the reviewed release images, then use the
+  [authentication migration cutover](../src/features/activities/providers/google/authorizationREADME.md#connection-generation-migration)
+  for releases that change Calendar authorization state. Compose's one-shot migration
+  dependency gates cold startup; it does not itself stop old application processes
+  before an upgrade migration runs. The connection-generation migration requires the
+  stopped-service sequence below that link, rather than an overlapping restart.
 - **Logs:** `docker compose logs -f app` (or `ws` / `worker` / `caddy`).
 - **Backups:** the database lives in the `pgdata` volume. Take a dump on a schedule, e.g.
   `docker compose exec -T postgres pg_dump -U warpdrive warpdrive | gzip > backup-$(date +%F).sql.gz`.
