+
+
+## 9. Authorized calendar continuation, 31 October 2026
+
+The earlier implementation deferral in section 8 is historical. The user subsequently authorized the full calendar implementation in its owned worktree and explicitly prioritized Google Calendar plus Meet. The persistent goal is active. [Current continuation evidence](calendar-progress-2026-11-01.md) separates local reminder delivery and defaults, dedicated OAuth/account infrastructure, HTTP contract tests and unfinished provider acceptance.
+
+The routine editor now follows a compact hierarchy: title and grouped schedule first, a visible calendar summary, on-demand time-zone/calendar options, then collapsed CRM details. Native settings remain functional and survive collapsing; non-default privacy/availability and authored zones stay visible. This is a Warpdrive refinement informed by official Google references and a read-only inspection of the current blank full editor on a personal English-UK account. That inspection establishes this one editor hierarchy only, not full Google parity, Workspace behavior or provider acceptance.
+
+Google HTTP contracts, dedicated consent/token persistence, session-bound OAuth routes and offboarding cleanup now have local synthetic-transport and PostgreSQL tests. The Settings > Connections account card, owner-scoped query and CSRF-protected local disconnect are implemented with 28 passing UI/boundary tests and current type/static checks. Browser acceptance, retention cleanup, provider mappings, sync/watch workers and actual Meet provisioning remain required. The user confirmed no provider test accounts/app registration are available yet and requested continued local implementation. No pasted URL or simulated response establishes external acceptance.
